  "comment": "Written by the daily sweep routine. It fires hourly from 08:00 Europe/Madrid and stops as soon as last_success matches today, so a failed run gets retried and a finished one does not repeat. Every create path (gh CLI, curl, GitHub MCP) appends a Claude Code footer to pull request bodies and comments, which this repo does not carry. Strip a pull request body afterwards with the MCP update_pull_request call, which does not re-append; verified on PR 96 on 5 November 2026. A COMMENT cannot be cleaned this way: both the REST PATCH and MCP update_issue_comment re-append the footer to a comment, also verified on PR 96, so a comment that must carry no signature cannot be posted at all. Put what it would have said in the pull request body instead, and delete the comment with DELETE /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/comments/{id} if one is already up. Note that a REST PATCH of a pull request body re-appends the footer too, so use the MCP call for that, not gh api. Verify the tail by reading the body back.",
